  "drivers": "Nasdaq-100 futures are down about 2.6% and S&P 500 futures about 1.1%, while Dow futures are roughly flat, as AI-spending and cash-flow worries spread a day after Alphabet's worst session in over 20 years. Intel is down ~26% after guiding Q4 revenue to $15–16B and EPS to $0.25, below estimates, and warning PC weakness could last into 1H 2027 (it also cited ~$300M lost from an Israel fab disruption); Dell and HP fall 12–13% in sympathy. Amazon is down ~7% after Q3 EPS of $1.89 missed $1.96, Q4 sales guidance came in below consensus, and trailing free cash flow swung to a record −$42.4B on $77B of quarterly capex; memory names (SanDisk −9%, Micron −6%, SK hynix −7%) and SOXX (−6.7%) slide, and Asian chips fell overnight (Kospi −3.9%, Nikkei −2.1%). Crypto stocks drop after Binance reported a ~$6.3B hack (bitcoin ~$77K, six-week low). Oil is up ~2% on reports the US may resume strikes on Iran and a tanker incident in the Strait of Hormuz; Treasury yields slip and gold falls below $4,000. The BoJ held at 1.25% overnight; euro-zone Q3 GDP beat (+0.4% q/q). At 7:30 a.m. CT, the Q3 Employment Cost Index rose 0.8%, in line (Q2 +0.9%). No Fed speakers were found on today's calendar.",
